WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.060
It's that time again.

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.900
Welcome to Tesla Short's Time, episode 550.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.140
I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.140
Today is July 23rd, 2026.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:12.860
Plenty going on in EV land.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:14.020
Let's get to it.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:17.840
Heavy spending on AI, robots, and robot axes

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.780
is squeezing Tesla's profits even as revenue

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:21.840
climbs to a record.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:26.560
Tesla reported record revenue and 25% delivery growth

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:27.300
in the quarter.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.980
Operating profits still declined as costs rose

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.720
from production delays on the cybercab, semi,

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.080
and mega pack programs, plus continued AI

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.520
and robotics investment.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:42.640
Battery pack capacity remains the main near-term limiter

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.480
on vehicle output, according to the earnings update.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.980
The company continues to bet that the same spending

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:52.560
will eventually expand margins once the new program's scale.

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:55.800
While the capital allocation debate plays out

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.920
at the company level, customers are already voting

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:01.820
with their wallets on one key software offering.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.880
Over 55% of North American Q2 deliveries

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:08.160
included an FSD subscription.

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:11.560
Tesla reported record attach rates at delivery

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:14.600
and record net new subscriptions in the same period.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:19.860
Version 14.3.6 introduces adjustable speed profiles

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:22.240
with a more conservative default behavior.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:25.820
Early user feedback highlights smoother responses

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:28.160
and human-like maneuvers during testing.

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:32.280
The V14 series continues the rapid iteration path

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:34.600
from V12 through V13.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:38.060
Listeners tracking FSD unsupervised

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:40.540
will watch whether later iterations loosen

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:44.040
the conservative settings once more real-world data arrives.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:47.440
Strong supervised adoption is feeding data

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.260
into the next phase of autonomy,

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:51.960
where the dedicated RoboTaxi fleet

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.800
is already running newer code.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:57.720
A dedicated cybercab assembly line is now visible

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:01.980
at Giga Texas after the Model S and X lines were decommissioned.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:04.840
A subset of those purpose-built vehicles

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:08.060
is already testing FSD version 15.

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:11.400
Musk stated during post-earnings discussion

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.880
that internal ride demand is sufficient

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:16.460
to skip partnerships with Uber or Waymo.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.920
This keeps the business model fully

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:21.320
inside Tesla's control and data loop.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:23.760
Regulators in the seven current metros

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:27.120
will determine how quickly that internal demand can scale.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.500
The setup directly addresses the open question

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:34.100
of how quickly purpose-built RoboTaxi volume can ramp

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:36.320
once regulatory approval arrives.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:40.260
The same software path now has a concrete timeline

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.860
for another vehicle program.

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:45.600
The Tesla semi remains on track for volume production

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.880
this year at the new Nevada factory.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:51.540
Musk told investors unsupervised capability

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:54.900
for the semi should arrive by early 2027

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:57.160
once the RoboTaxi stack matures.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:01.400
Autonomy is now the clearer gate versus hardware readiness.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.700
Fleet customers will watch whether

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.820
the shared software path accelerates

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:07.660
or delays commercial deployments.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:12.140
The timeline update directly addresses the tracked semi-program

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:14.780
where hardware production and software readiness

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:17.220
have been the two parallel open questions.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:21.440
Energy storage is also scaling hardware quickly,

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:23.740
though margins tell a different story.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:26.560
Tesla reported its strongest quarter yet

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:30.520
for Megapack and Powerwall deployments in EEMAE

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:33.580
supported by the Shanghai Megafactory ramp.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:38.760
Energy storage gross margins fell 19% due to higher input costs

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.080
and ramp expenses.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:43.800
The company is still on track to start Megapack 3

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:47.120
and Megablock production at the new Texas Megafactory

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.120
later this year.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.700
Investors will monitor whether the new factory's scale

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:54.320
reverses the margin pressure in coming quarters.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.840
Manufacturing preparation is also advancing

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.160
on the Robotic side.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:02.840
Tesla named TSMC, Samsung and Micron

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:06.520
as key optimist partners for compute, memory and packaging.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:10.420
First generation production lines are now under construction

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:13.440
at Fremont after the Model S and X assembly

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:14.500
was decommissioned.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:17.520
Early Optimus units will stay internal

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:21.600
for training data collection ahead of the 2027 volume target.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:25.400
This partnership list gives the first concrete view

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:29.040
of the supply chain behind the 2027 volume target.

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:31.920
All of these hardware programs ultimately

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:34.840
rest on the same expanding compute foundation.

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:38.800
Tesla more than doubled onsite AI training compute

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:41.620
in Texas during the first half of 2026.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.780
Cortex 2 is now supporting both vehicle

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:46.980
and humanoid autonomy development

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:49.740
and will continue to ramp through year end.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:53.020
The company acquired an AI hardware firm

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:55.980
for $1.95 billion in stock

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:58.320
to bolster semiconductor capabilities.

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:01.100
The deal closed in the second quarter

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.720
through an asset purchase paid in common stock

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:04.900
and equity awards.

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:08.440
The target remains unnamed but reports point

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:11.360
to semiconductor design or packaging capabilities

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:14.660
that could support AI5 and Dojo roadmaps.

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:18.360
The move adds in-house capacity at a time

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:20.160
when training and inference compute

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:22.680
are the main constraints on both FSD

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.300
and Optimus timelines.

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:27.060
Cortex 2 already supports vehicle

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:29.340
and humanoid autonomy development

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:33.220
following the first half doubling of onsite Texas compute.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:36.160
The increase comes alongside progress

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:38.380
on the Austin semiconductor fab.

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:43.340
The Supercharger network added more than 2,400 net new stalls

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:44.400
in the first half.

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:47.860
The network grew 17% year over year

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.280
while the company continues to open sites

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:51.760
to non-Tesla vehicles.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:55.140
Utilization data from the expanded network

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:57.940
will help determine whether open access improves

00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:00.160
or dilutes per stall economics.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:03.060
Expansion remains a supporting piece

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:06.200
of both vehicle and future robotaxi operations.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:09.060
The addition continues the steady build out

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:10.560
tracked in prior quarters.

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:14.480
FSD supervised was credited with saving lives

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:16.420
in a new Tesla post that highlighted

00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:18.900
real world interventions preventing collisions.

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:22.620
The post comes as attach rates hit record levels

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:23.620
in North America.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:27.280
It underscores the safety case the company is building

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:30.600
while regulators evaluate unsupervised operation.

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:33.180
The message aligns with the broader

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:37.140
supervised FSD safety report shared in the same period.

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:41.820
A Chinese influencer called FSD version 14 badass

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:46.540
after a US test drive in a model Y with HW-4 hardware.

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:50.000
Chen Zen compared the latest build favorably

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.980
to Chinese competitors after testing a model Y

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:54.800
with HW-4 hardware.

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:58.820
He highlighted human-like maneuvers such as backing up

00:06:58.820 --> 00:07:00.960
at a red light for a wide turning truck

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:03.280
and precise windshield wiper behavior.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:07.800
The shift in tone from his earlier Lukewarm V13 assessment

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:09.960
shows how quickly the supervised stack

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:11.560
is closing perceived gaps.

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:15.540
Both Mad Max and Sloth speed profiles delivered

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:19.080
the noted results during the FIFA World Cup trip test.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:22.620
Powerwall 3P is now available in Germany

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:25.540
for three phase homes as a single unit solution.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:29.020
The offering meets local electrical requirements

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:31.320
that previously needed multiple systems

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:33.300
and expands the addressable market

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.620
for residential storage paired with solar.

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:39.220
Early uptake will test whether the simplified offering

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:42.140
lifts attach rates in a key European market.

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:45.900
The launch follows the tracked Tesla energy program

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:48.080
where residential and utility products

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:50.820
have both seen recent geographic expansion.

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:54.660
Tesla semi remains on track for volume production

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:56.980
this year at the new Nevada factory,

00:07:57.260 --> 00:08:00.040
even as broader capital spending faces scrutiny.

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:02.460
Fleet customers are still waiting

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:05.040
for the first unsupervised capable units.

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:08.280
The timeline now hinges on software readiness

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:09.940
rather than hardware alone.

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:13.640
The Nevada facility addition keeps the semi program

00:08:13.640 --> 00:08:15.880
moving forward on the hardware side

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:19.680
while the new FSD timeline supplies the software milestone.

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:22.300
Now, one thing worth watching.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:26.340
Tesla warned that costs climbed after production delays

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:28.900
on cybercab, semi, and mega pack.

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:32.700
Operating profit dropped even though revenue reached

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:35.700
a record and deliveries rose 25%.

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:38.440
The company is betting that the same AI

00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:41.060
and robotics programs driving the spending

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:42.960
will eventually expand margins.

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:46.120
But near-term cash flow remains under pressure.

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:49.900
Battery pack capacity expansion was again cited

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:53.040
as the main near-term limiter on vehicle output.

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:56.520
Scaling three distinct hardware programs at once

00:08:56.520 --> 00:09:00.180
forces trade-offs that single product companies never face.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:04.060
Tesla is simultaneously ramping vehicle production,

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:07.040
building a purpose-built robot taxi fleet,

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:11.340
and installing optimist lines inside the same capital envelope.

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:14.280
Each program carries its own learning curve

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:18.240
on yield, supplier qualification, and regulatory approval,

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:21.700
yet they all draw from the same pool of engineering hours

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:22.460
and cash.

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:25.820
Battery pack capacity is already identified

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:29.180
as the binding constraint on near-term vehicle output.

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:33.280
So every additional dollar directed toward AI inference

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:36.060
silicon or humanoid actuators directly

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:37.660
competes without expansion.

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:41.100
The shared constraints create sequencing risk

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:44.720
where a delay in one area can star resources from the others.

00:09:45.260 --> 00:09:47.840
Investors are therefore paying for optionality

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:50.080
rather than near-term margin expansion.

00:09:50.840 --> 00:09:54.600
Whether the bet pays off depends less on any single program's

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:57.160
technical success and more on whether Tesla

00:09:57.160 --> 00:10:00.180
can sequence the three ramps without exhausting cash

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:01.800
or talent in the interim.

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:05.000
Keep an eye on the Texas mega-factory ramp

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:08.120
for any early signals on energy margin recovery.

00:10:08.740 --> 00:10:10.540
That's your Tesla news for today.

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:17.480
TSLA closed at $374.1 down $4.92.

